# Alpha Deck — Signals Lab (sig) environment template. Copy to `.env.sig` (gitignored) and fill in values.
#
# The Signals Lab is the THIRD isolated stack (beside prod + dev): an off-prod historical-replay/backtest
# tier. It runs FROM THE WORKTREE root:
#   docker compose -f docker-compose.yml -f docker-compose.sig.yml -p alphadeck_sig --env-file .env.sig up -d --build
# Compose injects the vars below into the sig backend container (same names/semantics as prod's `.env`). It
# is FINE to reuse prod's values here — sig reads the same external services; only the DB / ports / volumes
# are namespaced (alphadeck_sig). NEVER commit the real `.env.sig`; keep only this template.
#
# NB: because the lab runs FROM THE WORKTREE, there are NO SIG_BACKEND / SIG_FRONTEND path vars — `./backend`
# and `./frontend` in the compose files already point at the worktree's own dirs. This file carries only the
# live-feature secrets/config.

# --- The Anthropic API key for the LLM seams --------------------------------------------------------
# FAIL-OPEN: with no key the LLM seams simply return nothing and the rest of the app is unaffected.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# --- The SEC EDGAR User-Agent (filing pulls). Format: "Name contact@email" --------------------------
# Required for LIVE SEC pulls (e.g. a manual historical fundamentals backfill for the backtest); without it
# live pulls are skipped and cached/seed data still works.
ALPHADECK_USER_AGENT=Alpha Deck Research admin you@example.com

# --- OPTIONAL: a Polygon.io API key (the price / ETF-flow source the code reads) --------------------
# With a key, ETF fund shares-outstanding samples come from Polygon first; without one, the free scrapers
# cover the sample. Fail-open. Reuse prod's value.
POLYGON_API_KEY=

# --- OPTIONAL: an OpenFIGI API key (entity resolution; works key-less but rate-limited) -------------
# OPENFIGI_API_KEY=

# --- OPTIONAL: the deployment tenant (defaults to the demo tenant if unset) -------------------------
# ALPHADECK_TENANT_ID=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001

# NB: DATABASE_URL is intentionally NOT set here — the sig compose overlay hard-codes the in-network URL
#     (postgres:5432/alphadeck_sig). A `.env.sig` DATABASE_URL would only ever be for a host uvicorn loop.
# NB: the cron secrets (SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL, the cron schedule vars) are omitted — the sig cron is OFF (R16).
